    <briefdescription>
<para>A file system according to your operating system. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This may be linked to the process&apos;s working directory, or maintain its own.</para>
<para>Currently, its own working directory is emulated by storing the path and sending absolute paths to <ref refid="namespacellvm_1_1sys_1_1fs" kindref="compound">llvm::sys::fs</ref>:: functions. A more principled approach would be to push this down a level, modelling the working dir as an llvm::sys::fs::WorkingDir or similar. This would enable the use of openat()-style functions on some platforms. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
